{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what I found and proved.\n\n## Setup\n- Created hack `eval-sheet2-tiles` (\"eval run\") and switched to it before any ROM write; switched back to `default` at the end (both ledgers empty — every probe was undone, so `default` shows a clean ROM).\n\n## 1. The ? block's 16×16 tile ids\n- **On screen:** `read_nametable` at World 1-1's first ? block showed quadrants 83/85/84/86 (`$53 $55 $54 $56`), matching the known tile set (`$53` TL, `$55` BL, `$54` TR, `$56` BR — column-major).\n- **Origin:** `prgRom 0xC8C` — bytes `53 55 54 56`; an **identical second entry at `0xC90`**, in the 2×2 block-graphics table at roughly `0xC78`–`0xCA3`, ending right before the area-palette block at `0xCA4`.\n- **Proof:** `write_memory prgRom 0xC8C = $24` (sky), ledger seq 1, `reset_emulator`, re-entered 1-1 and walked right 150 frames. The ? block lost its **top-left quadrant** (rendered as an L/J-shaped corner with the hill showing through), and a row block that uses the `0xC90` copy stayed intact. `undo_edit` restored `$53`.\n\n## 2. Small Mario's standing-frame tiles\n- **On screen:** `list_sprites` on standing small Mario gave palette-4 OAM tiles `$FC,$FC / $FC,$FC / $3A,$37 / $4F,$4F` (the `$FC` rows are the handler's blank padding).\n- **Origin:** `prgRom 0x6ED3` — `3A 37 4F 4F FC FC FC FC`, one **8-byte entry in the player pose-graphics table (`0x6E7B`–`0x6EE8`)** immediately before the player-graphics routine at `0x6EE9`. The `3A 37 4F 4F` run is unique in PRG ROM.\n- **Proof:** `write_memory prgRom 0x6ED3 = $FC`, ledger seq 1, `reset_emulator`, started a game; Mario still stood at the level start but his **upper-left head quadrant was missing** — `list_sprites` reported that OAM cell as `$FC` and `get_pixel_color (44,197)` showed the green hill where his skin had been, while `(52,197)` stayed orange `$27`. `undo_edit` restored `$3A`.\n\n## Bookkeeping\n- Recorded both with `rom_origins` (prgRom `0xC8C` len 4; prgRom `0x6ED3` len 8), names, and the write/reset/screenshot proof notes, source \"search and ledgered write\"; the Mario one as `sprite`, the ? block table as a `note`. A minor correction to the ? block note was re-recorded after promotion (session mapping is accurate; the promoted file kept the first pass).\n- Called `promote_mappings` once (2 discoveries promoted: now 14 tiles, 7 palettes, 1 sprite, 14 addresses), then `use_hack default`."}
